          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "टोकरी (ṭokrī) — \"a basket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here the trail stops early. टोकरी (ṭokrī) has no agreed Sanskrit ancestor, and the retroflex ट at the front is the sound most often credited to old contact with the Dravidian languages of the south — the same honest gap you already met under पेट."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A टोकरी (ṭokrī) is woven, usually from split cane or from the ribs of a leaf, and it is what सब्ज़ी comes home from the बाज़ार in. Light, cheap, and mended rather than replaced."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
