        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: लकड़ी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लकड़ी (lakṛī) — \"wood, a stick of firewood\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Usually traced back to Sanskrit लगुड (laguḍa), 'a club, a staff', through a Prakrit form with a doubled consonant in the middle. A word for a stick you swing became the word for the stuff a stick is made of."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लकड़ी (lakṛī) is both, in fact: the material and one piece of it. A bundle of it under the arm is what feeds the चूल्हा, which is why this word and that one turn up in the same sentence more often than any other pair in this book."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: रस्सी (rassī), सूई (sūī), टोकरी (ṭokrī), मिट्टी (miṭṭī), लकड़ी (lakṛī). Enough to say what a working pair of hands is holding."
            }
          ]
        },
